   "notes": "Cold curve is at 0 K; Tr=296 K anchors thermal-pressure increments only. Absolute Debye thermal pressure excludes zero-point pressure. Gamma=0.5+2.2*(V/V0). Fit coverage is quasi-hydrostatic runs 2-3 plus pure argon below 5 GPa; pure-Ar compression to 114 GPa is a separate comparison. Low-temperature validation is below about 20 GPa, not the full P-T rectangle. Paper says 300 K in fitting prose although Methods report 296 K; both are audited. No fitted parameter errors or covariance reported. Supplement contains 5.5 K and 300 K rows beyond the headline 10-296 K range."
  },
