   "notes": "0 K cold curve includes zero-point energy; Debye thermal term excludes it. Marginal model/fit envelope 0-760 K and up to 6.3 GPa is not a rectangular solid-stability region; use solid branch below melting. New data cover 7.96-50.02 K only. Volume uncertainties estimated k=1: 0.1% sublimation, 0.5% melting/compressed; coefficient covariance/errors not published. Gas reference entropy 130.37 J/mol/K belongs to coupled fluid equilibrium model and does not enter solid pressure. No fluid fugacity/phase-equilibrium solver supplied. Complete global refit cannot be reconstructed from available files; workbook reference calculations are theory, not observations. The author workbook gas constant R=8.31451 J/mol/K is retained explicitly for published numerical parity. Record temperature_ref=70 K selects the evaluation/reporting temperature; it is not the cold-curve reference temperature, which is 0 K."
  }
